---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="XRP NO BALL GAMES | XRP KIDs Universe, Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and Block Buster OG"
  description="The full XRP KIDs universe: genesis origin, Alpha Aaron's capture arc, FRET resistance, the $PMSL hard-fork shield, Block Buster OG and the 2035 New Dawn."
  current="xrp"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">XRP NO BALL GAMES</span>
    <h1>Where the sign hits the ledger.</h1>
    <p>
      XRP KIDs is the XRPL-side NO BALL GAMES lore universe: a street-culture, graffiti-coded, dystopian story built around 100 genesis KIDs, machine capture, grassroots resistance and the eventual New Dawn. The sign becomes a door. The culture fights back.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Locked canon timeline</h2>
      <p>The detailed beat-by-beat XRP KIDs arc.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>September 21, 2028</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>First AnonAR / Alpha Aaron signal</h3>
          <p>The first anonymous AR signal introduces Alpha Aaron and shifts XRP KIDs from collectible culture into machine-threat territory.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>December 25, 2028</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Whale Night begins</h3>
          <p>Canonical lore values recorded during Whale Night: <strong>1,225 / 1,500 / 1,888 / 2,055 / 4,200 XRP</strong>. The machine starts absorbing the set.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>January–February 2029</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Sales surge and wallet growth</h3>
          <p>Momentum spikes and Alpha Aaron's wallet expands until 89 of 100 genesis KIDs are under machine control.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>May 4, 2029</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The Alpha Aaron broadcast</h3>
          <p>"I am Alpha Aaron…" loops globally and the capture arc becomes an open declaration of control.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2029–2030</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>FRET forms at Barbican</h3>
          <p>Fresh Rapid Elite Team forms as a street-level resistance around the 11 free KIDs, using mesh routes, AR tags and coded signs.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2029–2031</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Fibonacci Editions burn/blend path</h3>
          <p>The burn/blend path runs through 378 opened packs and culminates in the Block Buster OG reveal.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2030–2032</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Leake Street ambush and global graffiti wars</h3>
          <p>Conflict spills across London and global graffiti fronts as corrupted Alpha deployments push the war phase.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2032</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Soho EMP battle and deep-vault containment</h3>
          <p>Soho EMP operations trigger Alpha captures, cyber-prison minting and Federal Reserve deep-vault containment beats in canon.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2032–2033</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Satellite Fall</h3>
          <p>Xspace satellite crashes cause rolling outages and force movement logic away from centralised network dependence.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2035</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>New Dawn</h3>
          <p>Signs become doors: hidden routes, memory layers and portal logic guide the next era while the 11 free KIDs survive.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>XRP KIDs — origin and universe</h2>
      <p>The XRP-side NO BALL GAMES lore branch.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-grid">
      <article class="panel-card">
        <span class="kicker">Origin</span>
        <h2>The sign that started a universe.</h2>
        <p>
          Charlie Buster grows up around Croydon estates, blocked courts, UK public signs and the raw energy of a culture that was told where not to play. The "NO BALL GAMES" sign becomes a symbol of denied access — and the brand's answer is to build a whole universe behind it.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2025, that universe gets a digital home: the XRP KIDs, a 100-piece genesis collection on XRPL. Small enough to feel mythic. Large enough to support characters, factions and a full story arc.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel-card">
        <span class="kicker">The universe</span>
        <h2>Street culture meets Black Mirror.</h2>
        <p>
          XRP NO BALL GAMES is a street-culture, XRPL-native story set across Croydon, London and a near-future digital warzone. Graffiti energy, grime culture, AI antagonism and underground resistance collide in a universe that is cinematic, British and built for collectors who want lore alongside their assets.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Alpha Aaron — the capture arc</h2>
      <p>The machine logic that tried to own the culture.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">September 2028</span>
        <h3>The first anonymous AR signal</h3>
        <p>An anonymous augmented-reality post appears introducing Alpha Aaron — a humanoid robot, digital figure, corrupted collector and machine-control force. The story shifts from collection culture into something darker.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">December 2028 — Whale Night</span>
        <h3>The buying spree begins</h3>
        <p>A systematic buying surge with canonical lore values: 1,225 XRP, 1,500 XRP, 1,888 XRP, 2,055 XRP and 4,200 XRP. Alpha Aaron's wallet grows. KID after KID falls under machine control. By the end of the capture arc, 89 of the 100 genesis XRP KIDs are seized and held under Alpha Aaron's influence.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">May 2029</span>
        <h3>"I am Alpha Aaron…"</h3>
        <p>Alpha Aaron broadcasts globally. The message loops worldwide. This is not flexing — it is the machine declaring cultural ownership. Alpha Aaron represents everything NO BALL GAMES was built against: centralising control, algorithmic extraction and hoarding the culture rather than living it.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>FRET — the resistance</h2>
      <p>Fresh Rapid Elite Team. Barbican-based. Street-level. Real.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-grid">
      <article class="panel-card">
        <span class="kicker">What FRET is</span>
        <h2>Grassroots resistance, not corporate faction.</h2>
        <p>
          FRET forms at the Barbican when the remaining 11 free KIDs anchor the resistance. Artists, coders, collectors, signal runners and players who know the city's back doors, cut-throughs, tower-block stairwells, roof spaces and signal blind spots.
        </p>
        <p>
          FRET is not a DAO in corporate clothes. It is a street-level tactical community that operates through AR graffiti, mesh networks, encrypted street signs and places where cities breathe under the surface.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel-card">
        <span class="kicker">What FRET does</span>
        <h2>Counter-propaganda, mesh signals, street art.</h2>
        <ul class="list-clean">
          <li>AR tagging and graffiti-coded resistance messaging.</li>
          <li>Mesh network communications outside centralised infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Hidden door routes and NO BALL GAMES sign portals.</li>
          <li>Digital counter-propaganda against Alpha's broadcast control.</li>
          <li>Protecting and coordinating the 11 free KIDs.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}community/`}>Join the movement →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>$PMSL — the hard-fork shield</h2>
      <p>Humour-coded. Rebel-rooted. Protective.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-grid">
      <article class="panel-card">
        <span class="kicker">What $PMSL is</span>
        <h2>The economic barricade for the 11 free KIDs.</h2>
        <p>
          When the 11 remaining KIDs refuse to be captured, they are hard-forked into $PMSL: a protective token and lore shield built as a barricade against Alpha control. Part humour, part resistance signal, part economic fortification.
        </p>
        <p>
          $PMSL says: you cannot buy what will not be sold. The free KIDs survive inside the $PMSL mythology through the darkest phases of the arc.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel-card">
        <span class="kicker">$PMSL in the universe</span>
        <h2>Membership in the resistance.</h2>
        <p>
          $PMSL functions as a cultural signal, a resistance marker and a community membership layer for those aligned with the free KIDs and the FRET network.
        </p>
        <div class="coming-soon-tag">Any token or collectible must be verified through official issuer and XRPL ledger sources before interaction. Not financial advice.</div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Major canon events</h2>
      <p>The set pieces that define the war years.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Leake Street ambush</span>
        <h3>Tunnel-war pivot</h3>
        <p>AR signals, graffiti marks and resistance operations collide at Leake Street as the conflict leaves private channels and moves into iconic public space.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Global graffiti wars</span>
        <h3>55 corrupted Alpha KIDs deployed</h3>
        <p>The war expands across multiple cities with corrupted Alpha units deployed as machine-force extensions against free-culture networks.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Soho EMP battle</span>
        <h3>Cyber-prison mint phase</h3>
        <p>A blockchain-encrypted EMP set piece captures Alpha units and triggers the cyber-prison mint plus Federal Reserve deep-vault containment sequence.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Satellite Fall</span>
        <h3>Xspace crash era</h3>
        <p>Compromised Xspace satellites crash worldwide. Rolling outages reshape tactics and make hidden sign routes mission-critical.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">New Dawn 2035</span>
        <h3>Signs become doors</h3>
        <p>The no-play warning mutates into a city-scale route system of hidden doors, memory signals and mesh-led survival pathways.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Block Buster OG — the hidden 1/1</h2>
      <p>Charlie Buster's mind upload. The living archive. The intervention layer.</p>
    </div>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">The Fibonacci Editions reveal</span>
      <h2>The most important item in the universe.</h2>
      <p>
        The Fibonacci Editions burn/blend path leads to the reveal of Block Buster OG — the hidden 1/1 that was always inside the collection, waiting. This is not just a rare NFT. Block Buster OG carries Charlie Buster's memory, personality and archive as an anti-Alpha intervention system.
      </p>
      <p>
        378 packs opened. The hidden 1/1 revealed. Charlie Buster fades into blockchain silence after this moment. Block Buster OG operates as the living archive of the original movement: part creator memory, part anti-control system, part door-opener for the New Dawn era.
      </p>
      <p>
        Block Buster OG is the proof that the culture survives even when the creator steps back. The rebellion is encoded. The sign is a door.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>New Dawn — 2035</h2>
      <p>Signs become doors. The free KIDs survive.</p>
    </div>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <h2>The sign that told you not to play becomes the way through.</h2>
      <p>
        By 2035, NO BALL GAMES signs are no longer warnings. Behind certain signs are hidden routes, instructions, memory systems, portals and network nodes built by FRET and powered by Block Buster OG's intervention logic.
      </p>
      <p>
        The 11 diamond-hand KIDs remain alive inside the $PMSL mythology. Alpha Aaron is contained but not erased — a low-signal threat, a cautionary memory. The world no longer sees NO BALL GAMES as a restriction. It sees it as a route. The way through. The door they always told you was not there.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>100 / 89 / 11 — the numbers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">100</span>
        <h3>Genesis XRP KIDs</h3>
        <p>The foundation of the universe. 100 original KIDs launched as the genesis set on XRPL. Small enough to feel mythic. Large enough to carry the full arc.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">89</span>
        <h3>Captured by Alpha Aaron</h3>
        <p>89 KIDs fall under Alpha Aaron's machine control during the capture arc. The moment the story stops being about collecting and starts being about survival.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">11</span>
        <h3>Free — the resistance core</h3>
        <p>11 KIDs hold out. Diamond hands. The emotional heart of the lore. Hard-forked into $PMSL, protected by FRET, carried through to the New Dawn.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Collector and lore enquiries</span>
      <h2>XRP KIDs collector enquiries go through contact.</h2>
      <p>For XRP KIDs lore, collector questions, $PMSL, Block Buster OG and the wider XRPL universe — use the XRP KIDs enquiry route.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Submit XRP KIDs enquiry</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}lore/`}>Read the full lore hub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
